1c:T760,<p>“What does a website cost?” is the most common question in a first consultation — and the honest answer is: it depends on what it’s supposed to achieve. That sounds evasive, but it’s the heart of the matter. A website isn’t an off-the-shelf product; it’s a tool with a job to do.</p>
<h2 id="the-three-price-brackets--and-what-you-get">The three price brackets — and what you get</h2>
<p><strong>Under €1,000: site builders.</strong> Wix, Squarespace and the like are legitimate for getting started. You pay with limited performance, interchangeable design and a ceiling on everything that comes later: SEO, extensions, speed.</p>
<p><strong>€2,500–8,000: custom-built by a professional.</strong> Most SME projects live in this range. Custom design, clean code, a CMS for self-service editing, an SEO foundation. This is where it’s decided whether your website is a cost center or a sales channel.</p>
<p><strong>€10,000+: complex requirements.</strong> Online shops with inventory systems, portals, custom web applications. If you receive quotes like this for a five-page website, ask for the reasoning.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-recognize-a-fair-quote">How to recognize a fair quote</h2>
<p>A serious quote answers three questions: What exactly will be delivered? What does it cost — as a fixed price? And what happens after launch? Be wary of hourly estimates without a cap, of “SEO included” without specifics, and of agencies that talk design before they know your goals.</p>
<h2 id="the-real-question-what-does-a-bad-website-cost">The real question: what does a bad website cost?</h2>
<p>Quick math: if your website brings in just two more qualified leads per month and your average order value is €2,000, a €6,000 website pays for itself in six weeks. The most expensive website is the one that achieves nothing — no matter how little it cost.</p>4:["$","main",null,{"id":"main","children":[["$","article",null,{"children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 md:px-8","style":{"paddingTop":"clamp(7.5rem, 12vw, 10rem)"},"children":[[["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"You are here","className":"text-[0.82rem]","children":["$","ol",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-mute","children":[["$","li","0-Home",{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[false,["$","a",null,{"href":"/en","className":"link-slide tap-24","children":"Home"}]]}],["$","li","1-Blog",{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":"/"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/en/blog","className":"link-slide tap-24","children":"Blog"}]]}],["$","li","2-What does a professional website cost in 2026? An honest answer",{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":"/"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-current":"page","className":"text-ink font-semibold","children":"What does a professional website cost in 2026? An honest answer"}]]}]]}]}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://surhay.design/en\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Blog\",\"item\":\"https://surhay.design/en/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"What does a professional website cost in 2026? An honest answer\"}]}"}}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-mute","child